Z||000000||MR2KLR||12-14-2001||12:22 PM||||<BR>My 88 coupe seems to have Low oil pessure What should it be for a 4-cyl? I think when I change the oil this saturday I'm going to use 20W50 or 50W oil that should help right? the car seems to run very strong (90k) I think it may be the oil pump takeing a dump on me. Could I replace one on jack stands?<P>Thanks<BR>tom<P>------------------<BR>  <BR>Black 88 Coupe: 120 MPH spedo, Aux. gauge pod, 195/55VR14 Potenza RE-71 tires, GT exhaust & ground F/X Soon to have 16" White Beretta GTZ W/ 215/45ZR16's<BR><A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||9
Z||000001||deceler8||12-14-2001||12:28 PM||||Don't go to ultra-heavy oil in an attempt to just increase the gauge reading because it's more likely the sensor is bad.<P>And heavier oil won't flow well in cool or cold weather, which will increase start-up wear.<P>If it ain't ticking or knocking, it's most likely the oil pressure sensor that's bad, not the oil pump.||||reg||1
