Z||000011||ToddAsh||12-14-2001||05:59 PM||||20W50 is not thick oil.Try straight 30W .On my big block Chevy I have to run straight 40W to maintain a decent pressure at idle.20W50 is 20W oil that protects like 50W when fully warm.If your weathers not too cold 30W should give you increased pressure without any hard starting.Todd||||reg||1
Z||000012||camon||12-15-2001||04:00 AM||||I'm also pondering using heavier oil (for like a month now) but am not 100% sure that it will be a good thing with the weather here in Pa going cold (it can get in the low teens or even single digits when winter finally does hit).<P>I'm currently using 10w30 (Pennzoil) and thinking about going to a 40 wieght...would this cause any harm to the V6 engine. My Fiero currently has 110k on it (and seems to run very strong). But as the engine warms up I notice a drastic drop in oil pressure while at idle (right around red....between 15-20psi). However when i'm in motion the pressure is right at bout 40psi (sometimes slightly higher). This thing has been like this since I got it (about 3 months now) and don't want to make things worse by adding too heavy an oil!<P>Should I do it (will it help or hurt)???....or do what I wanted to do but hate like hell to do.......high volume oil pump (i'm so sick of messing with pumps.....water pump, fuel pump and now possibly oil pump)???<P>------------------<BR>   Keith<BR>1987 Fiero GT||||reg||5
